<title>USA: Calif. Financing Authority repriced, yields cut.</title>
<headline>Calif. Financing Authority repriced, yields cut.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bear, Stearns &amp; Co., Inc. said Thursday it repriced and restructured California Financing Authority's $47 million bond deal, cutting yields in several maturities and eliminating the 2016 maturity.</p>
<p>The repricing/restructure follows:</p>
<p>FINANCING AUTHORITY FOR RESOURCE EFFICIENCY OF</p>
<p>RE: $47,155,000*</p>
<p>CALIFORNIA</p>
<p>CERTIFICATES OF PARTICIPATION, 1997 SERIES</p>
<p>(CAPITAL IMPROVEMENTS PROGRAM)</p>
<p>VERBAL AWARD.</p>
<p>WE WILL TAKE ORDERS FOR 2008 THROUGH 2012 ONLY UNTIL 2:30</p>
<p>P.M., E.D.S.T., TODAY, THURSDAY, APRIL 24, 1997 ON</p>
<p>(212)272-4910.</p>
<p>PLEASE NOTE 2008 THROUGH 2012 ARE NON-CALLABLE AND CHANGE IN</p>
<p>COUPON</p>
<p>2013-2015, 2017 AND 2022.</p>
